  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#windoworworkerglobalscope-mixin:windoworworkerglobalscope-5\r\n\r\n> 6. Initialize event's ctrlKey, shiftKey, altKey, and metaKey attributes according to the current state of the key input device, if any \\(false for any keys that are not available\\)\\.\r\n\r\nand\r\n\r\n> 8. event's getModifierState() method is to return values appropriately describing the current state of the key input device.\r\n\r\nI kind of doubt that if I hold down <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> while the page calls `.click()`, that the resulting event will have `ctrlKey` set. If that is true (and we should test), it's quite surprising and the spec should note it.\r\n\r\nIf it's not true, as I suspect, then we need to fix up the definition of `.click()`.",
